{
  "statement": "Trustworthiness is vital in the library management system to safeguard member data and ensure secure operations. My requirements (TRU-01 to TRU-07) focus on authentication, logging for auditability, and data protection. TRU-01 ensures only authenticated members can borrow or return books, while TRU-03 enforces encryption for personal data. I raise concerns about SafetyAgent's SAF-06, which also addresses authentication but may overlook broader data protection measures. Furthermore, EfficiencyAgent's EFF-05 overlaps with TRU-05 regarding overdue notifications but lacks a focus on secure management of such notifications.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-06", "TRU-01"],
      "type": "redundant",
      "description": "Both requirements focus on authentication, but TRU-01 emphasizes broader security measures."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-05", "TRU-05"],
      "type": "redundant",
      "description": "Both requirements address overdue notifications, but TRU-05 emphasizes secure management."
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
    {
      "id": "SAF-06",
      "stance": "oppose",
      "proposal": "Integrate with TRU-01 to ensure comprehensive authentication measures."
    },
    {
